commit:  3e84853e2e5d60540a5022b64895d496910144eb
date:    2026-11-12
subject: perf: streamline apple asset downloads and caching

Build with scripts/build-ipatool.sh. It clones upstream into ipatool-fork/src
(gitignored), checks out the commit above, copies storefront_static.go into
pkg/appstore/, applies the three patches and builds bin/ipatool.

If proxy.golang.org is unreachable from your network, run it with
GOPROXY=direct GOSUMDB=off.

The directory is named src, not upstream: on a case-insensitive filesystem a path
like ipatool-fork/upstream collides with this UPSTREAM file.

Patches:
  storefront-fix.patch   static storefront table fallback + iTunes UA (needs
                         storefront_static.go copied in first)
  version-probe.patch    get-version-metadata reports minimumOS and more without a
                         full download. Mac packages: ranged probe of the XAR table
                         of contents and the chunk-aligned tail (upstream downloads
                         the entire package), adding architectures, bundleVersion,
                         packageSize, bytesFetched and a --probe-only flag. IPAs:
                         MinimumOSVersion, CFBundleVersion and device families from
                         the Info.plist upstream already reads by range.
  profiles.patch         IPATOOL_PROFILE=<name> isolates an Apple ID: its own keychain
                         service (ipatool-auth.service.<name>) and state directory
                         (~/.ipatool/profiles/<name>). Unset keeps stock storage, so
                         the existing session is the default profile.
